# Ready-made requests for the VS Code extension "REST Client" (humao.rest-client).
# Click "Send Request" above a request to send it.

@base = http://localhost:3000

### Example: list all sessions
GET {{base}}/api/sessions

### Example: create a session
POST {{base}}/api/sessions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "My own session",
  "speaker": "Kim Larsson",
  "room": "Room B",
  "startsAt": "2026-11-20T15:00",
  "endsAt": "2026-11-20T15:45",
  "capacity": 10
}

### Task 1: get a session
GET {{base}}/api/sessions/s1

### Task 1: session that does not exist (404)
GET {{base}}/api/sessions/s999

### Task 2: delete a session (204)
DELETE {{base}}/api/sessions/s8

### Task 3: update a session
PATCH {{base}}/api/sessions/s2
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "REST for real (updated)"
}

### Task 3: invalid body (400)
PATCH {{base}}/api/sessions/s2
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "capacity": -5
}

### Task 4: register an attendee
POST {{base}}/api/sessions/s3/registrations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Kim Larsson",
  "email": "kim@example.com"
}

### Task 4: invalid email (400)
POST {{base}}/api/sessions/s3/registrations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Kim Larsson",
  "email": "not-an-email"
}

### Task 5: list registrations
GET {{base}}/api/sessions/s4/registrations

### Task 7: s4 has 3 seats and 2 registrations – this one takes the last seat…
POST {{base}}/api/sessions/s4/registrations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Dana Ek",
  "email": "dana@example.com"
}

### Task 7: …and now it is fully booked (409)
POST {{base}}/api/sessions/s4/registrations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Eli Strom",
  "email": "eli@example.com"
}

### Task 8: already registered (anna is already registered for s1)
POST {{base}}/api/sessions/s1/registrations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Anna Karlsson",
  "email": "anna@example.com"
}

### Task 9: schedule conflict (ben is registered for s4 10:30–11:15, s3 runs 10:00–10:45)
POST {{base}}/api/sessions/s3/registrations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Ben Olsson",
  "email": "ben@example.com"
}
